// ────────────── Named Workspaces ──────────────
// https://github.com/YaLTeR/niri/wiki/Configuration:-Named-Workspaces
//
// Three persistent, named workspaces. Unlike the dynamic workspaces these
// always exist, and they take the low indices — so Mod+1/2/3 reach them while
// Mod+4.. still cover the dynamic ones that keep spawning below for terminals
// and everything else.
//
// Index order note: on a fresh niri start these follow declaration order
// (web=1, code=2, chat=3). A live config-reload instead inserts each named
// workspace at the top as it is read, so mid-session they can show reversed
// (chat=1, code=2, web=3) until the next login. This is cosmetic only — the
// open-on-workspace rules below match by NAME, so app routing is identical
// either way.
//
// Apps are steered onto these by open-on-workspace rules in cfg/rules.kdl:
// zen → web, GoLand / VSCode Insiders → code, Beeper → chat. Terminals are
// deliberately left unassigned; kitty is spread across many workspaces and
// pinning it would fight that.

workspace "web"
workspace "code"
workspace "chat"
